{"id":"audit-findings","title":"City-paid organizations whose federal audits reported findings","tier":"OFFICIAL","question":"When an independent auditor checked how these organizations handled federal money, did it report that rules or controls were not met, and did the same problem come back?","finding":"Federal audits are on file for 161 City-paid organizations (816 audit reports, 2019 to 2025). Auditors reported findings at 43 of them, and at 7 in three or more separate years; those 7 were paid $351 million by the City since FY2019. 22 of the 122 findings were marked as repeats of an earlier one, 30 were graded material weaknesses and 16 involved questioned costs. 3 parent organizations that file one audit covering several City payees (hospital systems among them) are listed last and left out of these counts.","how":"Each audit filed with the Federal Audit Clearinghouse was matched to a City payee by federal tax number, or by exact name where the City file has no number (marked). The federal file repeats a finding once for every grant it touches, so findings are counted once per audit and reference number. \"Through the City\" counts findings on a grant the auditor listed as passed through the City and County of San Francisco.","limits":"A finding is the auditor saying a requirement or control was not met; it is not a finding of fraud, and most are fixed. Hospital systems and other parents file one audit for the whole system, so a finding there may have nothing to do with the San Francisco payee (the \"one audit covers\" column names these). The file marks questioned costs yes or no and gives no dollar figure. For the fiscal years covered here, the federal audit threshold depends on the start of the entity’s fiscal year. It was $750,000 in federal awards expended across all programs for years starting before October 1, 2024, and $1 million for years starting on or after that date. An entity reaches the threshold at either amount. City payments alone cannot establish how much federal funding the recipient expended.","columns":[{"k":"org","t":"Organization","type":"org"},{"k":"covers","t":"One audit covers","type":"text"},{"k":"cityPaid","t":"City paid, FY2019 on","type":"usd"},{"k":"auditYears","t":"Years audited","type":"int"},{"k":"yearsWithFindings","t":"Years with findings","type":"int"},{"k":"years","t":"Which years","type":"text"},{"k":"findings","t":"Findings","type":"int"},{"k":"repeat","t":"Repeats","type":"int"},{"k":"materialWeakness","t":"Material weaknesses","type":"int"},{"k":"questionedCosts","t":"Questioned costs","type":"int"},{"k":"viaCity","t":"On money through the City","type":"int"},{"k":"matchedBy","t":"Matched by","type":"text"},{"k":"link","t":"Audit","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"org":"Marin City Health & Wellness Center","orgKey":"MARIN CITY HEALTH WELLNESS CENTER","covers":"","cityPaid":1010137,"auditYears":7,"yearsWithFindings":6,"years":"2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2024, 2025","findings":11,"repeat":4,"materialWeakness":3,"questionedCosts":1,"viaCity":0,"matchedBy":"tax number","link":{"t":"2025 audit summary","u":"https://app.fac.gov/dissemination/summary/2025-06-GSAFAC-0000412583"}},{"org":"PRC","orgKey":"PRC","covers":"","cityPaid":52942984,"auditYears":7,"yearsWithFindings":5,"years":"2019, 2020, 2021, 2022, 2024","findings":7,"repeat":4,"materialWeakness":0,"questionedCosts":0,"viaCity":7,"matchedBy":"tax number","link":{"t":"2024 audit summary","u":"https://app.fac.gov/dissemination/summary/2024-06-GSAFAC-0000371983"}},{"org":"Asian & Pacific Islander Wellness Center","orgKey":"ASIAN PACIFIC ISLANDER WELLNESS CENTER","covers":"","cityPaid":45864224,"auditYears":7,"yearsWithFindings":5,"years":"2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024","findings":7,"repeat":4,"materialWeakness":0,"questionedCosts":0,"viaCity":0,"matchedBy":"tax number","link":{"t":"2024 audit summary","u":"https://app.fac.gov/dissemination/summary/2024-03-GSAFAC-0000366177"}},{"org":"Baker Places Inc","orgKey":"BAKER PLACES","covers":"","cityP